gU0(){return"Worked out from where the arrows landed, as in the KPI method for coaches.\n\nPosition (bias): where the centre of the group sits compared with the centre of the face. It is fixed with the sight or the setup.\n\nAverage error (MAE): how far the arrows are from the centre on average, without sign. It holds both the aim and the consistency.\n\nConsistency (MAE-B): the same, measured from the centre of the group. It tells only how repeatable the shot is: the lower, the steadier.\n\nScatter (\u03c3): the standard deviation, how wide the group is. Arrows far out weigh more.\n\nA high average error with a low consistency figure means a tight group in the wrong place: adjust the sight. A high consistency figure calls for work on technique. Compare sessions at the same distance only."},
