gFv(){return"The time at anchor (TUT, time under tension) goes from the moment the hand reaches the anchor to the release. A companion or the coach takes it with the stopwatch.\n\nWindows of the KPI method: barebow 2.8\u20133.5 s, recurve 3\u20134 s, compound 4\u20136 s. In the window: the share of arrows inside it.\n\nWhat matters most is the variability: green up to 0.3 s, yellow up to 0.5 s, red beyond (intermediate level). A time that gets shorter is the hurry to let go; one that gets longer is the fear of the release; one that jumps from short to long is often the first sign of target panic, before it shows on the face."},
